    {
      "id": 197819,
      "name": "The Burning Stickman",
      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-05-07T16:40:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Nothing that's incapacitated or otherwise destroyed can do damage, unless that damage is the direct result of the process of it being destroyed (as with Sonic Mine).</p><p>If you kill, say, the Genebound Frosthound before it's hit every hero target, it stops dealing damage.</p><p>Same reason you don't see any hero Incap abilities that say, \"You do one target X damage.\" It's always, \"One hero target can do X damage,\" or \"one villain target does X damage to itself.\"</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:25:37.058Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 2,
      "readers_count": 1,
      "score": 0.4,
      "yours": false,
